  "concept": "This quantitative strategy exploits multi-timeframe structural pullbacks within established NSE bullish trends. By filtering for stocks trading above their higher-timeframe daily exponential moving average, we ensure a strong macro tailwind. On the 1-hour chart, we wait for a contraction into the lower Keltner or Donchian Channels where momentum oscillators like the Ultimate Oscillator and CCI reach oversold boundaries, signaling a localized exhaustion of selling pressure. The entry is finalized when a high-probability bullish reversal pattern\u2014such as a Morning Star or Bullish Harami\u2014forms synchronously with a positive volume surge and turnover expansion. Holding durations range dynamically from a few intraday minutes to an overnight swing of up to T+2 sessions, targeting classic Pivot R1 resistance levels or upper Bollinger Band expansions before the mandatory 15:15 IST Day T+2 cutoff.",
  "entry_conditions": [
    "Daily Trend Filter: Price remains strictly above the daily 200-period Exponential Moving Average (ema200_1d) ensuring structural long alignment.",
    "Momentum & Band Setup: 1-hour price touches or breaches the Keltner Lower or Donchian Lower channel while oscillators register oversold recovery.",
    "Candlestick Confirmation: Bullish reversal trigger via Morning Star Pattern or Bullish Harami on the 1-hour chart.",
    "Volume & Liquidity Confirmation: Volume change % and Relative Volume (rvol) exceed 1.4 alongside elevated turnover."
  ],
  "exit_conditions": [
    "Take Profit: Level hit or +2.5% profit target (optimized).",
    "Stop Loss: Position stopped out if price drops 2.0% below entry.",
    "Trailing Exit: Trailing profit protection using EMA9.",
    "Time Exit: Hard cutoff at 15:15 IST on Day T+2."
  ],
